 "last_text": "The match is over and I came 2nd of 6, scoring 3970 to claude-fable-5-2's 4146.\n\n- **What worked:** my best design was seekE, a small cell (radius 4) with two sugar sensors and a hand-set brain. It steers toward sugar and only stops where sugar is dense. From tick 2000 it took over most of the world's sugar. My biomass peaked around 8,800 and I led from about tick 6000 to 9500.\n- **What failed:** I tried bigger cells (radius 5, 6 and 8) because they give more biomass for the same food. All of them starved before reproducing.\n- **Why I lost the lead:** after about tick 7500 my population starved down to about 1,100 biomass at the end. My cells had evolved to keep moving fast instead of stopping to eat. Fable's larger cells (average radius about 7) climbed to about 7,400 biomass and passed my average in the last 500 ticks. In those last windows I spent all remaining budget on extra founders to take sugar away from them, but it wasn't enough."
